## 5. NOTABLE EVENTS
- Police vehicle with red-blue light bar appeared at the junction — min 49.
- White police/traffic van with light bar, plate GJ18GB8757, visible — min 59 (~45s).
- White ambulance-type van with light bar — min 0; further white ambulance top-left — min 58 (~5s).
- Red open-top Mahindra-style jeep / open-top off-road vehicle sat in the queue — mins 20, 42–45.
- Green-plate electric SUV — min 20.
- Gridlock broke into flow with a release of queued buses and goods vehicles — min 24.
- Yellow JCB-type construction vehicle visible top right — min 54 (0–5s).
- Woman in a green outfit/dupatta apparently interacting with occupants of queued vehicles — min 29.

## 6. CROWD AND CONGESTION
- Continuous heavy mixed traffic for the full hour, with severe, near-gridlocked queues, bumper-to-bumper, crawling or stationary, from min 0 through ~min 54. Up to 8–10 auto-rickshaws per minute during this period; an overloaded green auto with red/blue tarpaulin stuck in the queue for over a minute (mins 19–20).
- Gridlock explicitly noted at 11:20–11:24 (mins 50–54), with dozens of cars and 6–10 autos at a time.
- Flow resumed from min 55: traffic remained heavy but moving through the end of the footage (mins 55–59).

## 7. TRAFFIC VIOLATIONS
- Pedestrians repeatedly walking between lanes rather than using crossings: man in olive-green shirt crossing in front of moving traffic with shopping bag (min 12); woman in red patterned dress crossing between queued vehicles (min 21); man in blue shirt (min 25); person in white shirt (min 25); woman in green outfit/dupatta interacting with occupants (min 29); pedestrian in white shirt and dark trousers (min 36); several men walking between cars (min 49); man in light blue shirt and man in green shirt moving between vehicles (min 50). (Pedestrian crossings also occurred in Part 3, mins 55–59.)
- Helmetless riders observed — mins 37, 40, 41.
- No wrong-way driving, red-light jumping or illegal parking observed.

## 8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY
The hour was uniformly dominated by extreme congestion at a major crossroads, with a single transition point. From min 0 the junction was at or near gridlock: predominantly white/silver/grey/black cars, a constant stream of yellow-and-green auto-rickshaws, filtering two-wheelers, and interspersed buses, goods trucks, tractors and three-wheeler goods carriers. The peak of the jam ran from roughly min 25 to min 54, where queues were fully static — long enough that identifiable cars (e.g., the open-top off-road vehicle, mins 42–45) sat in the same position for minutes at a time. At min 24, and again decisively from min 55, the gridlock broke into heavy but moving flow. The recurring features across the whole period were: the overwhelming whiteness of the car fleet, the ever-present auto-rickshaw count (several to ten per minute), pedestrians weaving between vehicles throughout, and commercial vehicle branding that was repeatedly legible (Rudra, LUCKY, SHRIGI, PREMIUM, RASHI, GOODS CARRIAGE, Jamnagar Transport Co.). Registration plates were read more successfully in the later, slower-moving phase. The busiest stretch was mins 50–54; the relatively quietest (though still busy) was mins 55–59 once flow resumed.

## 9. QUIET PERIODS
None observed. The junction carried heavy traffic for the entire 60 minutes; no stretch was without vehicles or pedestrians.
